UNLICENSED - Proprietary and Confidential.

The Provian Commons is a reference implementation of the public institutional
layer. It is part of Provian's closed ("wallet + commons") surface and is NOT
open-sourced: it may not be copied, modified, distributed, or otherwise used
without the prior written consent of Provian Technologies, LLC.

The Provenance Envelope (PE) protocol that the Commons is built on IS open. The
open, permissively-licensed surface is the protocol and developer tooling -
`@provian/agent-sdk`, `@provian/cli`, `@provian/mcp`, the published PE
specification, and the relay's public API contract. Build an alternative Commons
on those open primitives; this reference implementation itself stays proprietary.

See the repository root `LICENSE` and `OPEN_SOURCE_SPLIT.md` for the full
open/closed boundary.
